    },
    "body": "Depends supports building packages from a local directory by creating an archive in `SOURCES_PATH`.\r\n\r\nThe archive filename was derived only from the relative local directory path. As a result, different worktrees using a shared `SOURCES_PATH` could refer to the same archive. If the archive created by one worktree was newer than all paths in another, the second worktree would reuse source contents from the first.\r\n\r\nInclude a shortened hash of the absolute local source path in the archive filename. This gives different worktrees separate archives and fetched stamps while retaining the existing mtime-based invalidation.\r\n\r\nThis approach is as suggested by ryanofsky in #35764. It therefore does not change the general mtime-based invalidation model.\r\n\r\nAddresses #35764",
